From 67695a16457e4d8ca53ee9c9a80a053ffcc0c39c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:29:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: pin log_line_prefix for the regression suite

The suite inspects `log_line_prefix` directly, five times, because the
extension prepends an audit tag to it:

    SHOW log_line_prefix;
     log_line_prefix
    -----------------
     %m [%p]

That expected value is PostgreSQL's built-in default, which is what the suite
sees when it runs against a server configured by hand. It is not what a
pg_regress `--temp-instance` provides: pg_regress writes its own
`log_line_prefix` into the temporary server's configuration so that its logs
identify the backend and application, and the suite then reports five diffs
against a setting nothing in the extension touched.

Ship the value the transcript expects as a config fragment a caller can hand
to pg_regress as a `--temp-config`, which is applied after pg_regress's own
settings and so wins. Nothing else in the suite depends on the prefix, and a
run against a hand-configured server is unaffected.
---
 hermetic.conf | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
 create mode 100644 hermetic.conf

diff --git a/hermetic.conf b/hermetic.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6e900c9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/hermetic.conf
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+log_line_prefix = '%m [%p] '
